==========================================================================
VERDICT
==========================================================================
  Algorithm 3.1 converged on 303/303 runs, every starting vector, every damping factor.

  Speed-up over the power iteration, by family of starting vector:
                     ones   d=0.85:  3.19x   d=0.95:  5.67x   d=0.99: 13.06x
      random non-negative   d=0.85:  3.28x   d=0.95:  5.79x   d=0.99: 13.16x
            random signed   d=0.85:  2.69x   d=0.95:  3.84x   d=0.99:  5.55x

  The headline result is robust to any NON-NEGATIVE start, which is the
  only kind that means anything for PageRank: scores are a distribution.
  Under the paper's signed stress test the dynamic method slows down and
  becomes more variable than the static one - the same sensitivity the
  paper itself reports in its Table 1. It still beats the power iteration.

