wrote result/exp8_limitations_spectrum.csv and _runs.csv
  wrote figure/exp8_limitations.pdf and .png

==========================================================================
THE BOUNDARY OF THE RESULT
==========================================================================
  Works   : undirected graphs. Real spectrum, every rival folded onto
            sqrt(beta), 3.2x-42x measured across 25 PageRank problems.
  Fails   : directed graphs. Complex spectrum, rivals escape the circle,
            and Algorithm 3.1 diverges at every damping factor tested.
  Cause   : one structural property - whether the graph has direction.

  This is a statement about the Google matrix, not about our code:
  experiment 1 reproduces the paper's own benchmarks, and the plain
  power iteration converges normally on web-Stanford throughout.

